    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know it sounds crazy but it's not like a headache or anything, it's too structured. like, yesterday i saw this massive indigo wash in the corner of my eye and five minutes later a huge tree limb fell right where i was walking. it feels less like a medical issue and more like my brain is suddenly picking up on data that's always been there but was just outside my sensory range. if we look at the math of wave-function collapse, is it possible that the exposure actually sensitized my neural pathways to detect these fluctuations before they manifest in macro reality?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
